use std
into fold_check.amni

```amni
import os;
import gfx;
import math;
import gfx.linalg;
import gfx.gltf;
import gfx.motion;
import gfx.scene3d;
import clips;
import mix;
import spring;
```

Vertex helpers. Each vertex g starts at `b = g * gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS` in `gltf::verts`. `vp(g int) float3` is the rest point (gltf::verts[b], gltf::verts[b + 1], gltf::verts[b + 2]) and `vn(g int) float3` the rest normal at b + 3, b + 4, b + 5. `skp(g int, m gfx::mat4[:]) float3` is the linear-blend skinned point: start from zero and for q in 4, with `w = gltf::verts[b + 22 + q]`, when w > 0 add `linalg::point(m[gltf::verts[b + 18 + q] as int], vp(g)) * w`. `skn(g int, m gfx::mat4[:]) float3` is the skinned normal: with p = vp(g) and n = vn(g), for the same four influences add `(linalg::point(mm, p + n) - linalg::point(mm, p)) * w` where mm is that joint's matrix, then return `linalg::unit3` of the sum. When `cor_on` is true and `CH[g]` is true, both use the center-of-rotation skin instead: blend the joint rotations `JQ[j]` of the four influences with weight w > 0 (negate a quaternion whose four-component dot product with the first influence's quaternion is negative, sum x, y, z and w times w, then `linalg::qnorm`) into q; skp returns `linalg::qrotate(q, vp(g) - CR[g])` plus the sum over the influences of `linalg::point(m[j], CR[g]) * w`, and skn returns `linalg::unit3(linalg::qrotate(q, vn(g)))`.

Globals: `bt int[>..]` (three global vertex ids per skin triangle), `ra f32[>..]` (rest area per triangle), `rb int[>..]` (body region per triangle), `let NB = 8` regions, `var h0 f32 = 1.0e30` and `var h1 f32 = -1.0e30` (rest height range of the skin vertices), `pal gfx::mat4[>..]` (joint matrices), `var sk_i = -1` (the skin index) , `var dump = false`, `var cor_on = false`, `CR float3[>..]` and `CH bool[>..]` (center of rotation and whether it exists, indexed by global vertex id and sized to `gltf::verts.len / gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS`), and `JQ linalg::Quat[>..]` (the rotation of each joint matrix in the current pose).

`region(name const byte[:]) int` maps a joint name to a body region by its prefix: 0 for "pelvis" or "thigh", 1 for "calf", "foot" or "ball", 2 for "spine", 3 for "clavicle" or "upperarm", 4 for "lowerarm", 5 for "hand", "index", "middle", "pinky", "ring" or "thumb", 6 for "neck" or "head", else 7. `rname(r int) const byte[:]` returns "hips+thighs", "legs", "torso", "shoulders", "forearms", "hands", "neck+head" or "other" for 0 to 7.

`gather(asset int, name const byte[:])` collects one mesh. `let nd = gltf::find_node(asset, name)`; when nd < 0 print "no node " and the name and return. Set `sk_i = gltf::nodes[nd].skin`. With `let ms = gltf::meshes[gltf::nodes[nd].mesh]`, for pi in ms.prims.count take `let pr = gltf::prims[ms.prims.first + pi]`: for v in pr.vcount update h0 and h1 with the min and max of `vp(pr.vfirst + v).y`; for q in pr.icount push `pr.vfirst + gltf::indices[pr.ifirst + q] as int` onto bt. Then for each triangle t (corners bt[3t], bt[3t + 1], bt[3t + 2] with rest points a, b, c) push the rest area `0.5 * linalg::length3(linalg::cross(b - a, c - a))` onto ra and its region onto rb: sum the weights per joint slot over the three corners (corner g has joint slots `gltf::verts[g * gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS + gltf::AT_JOINT + k] as int` with weights `gltf::verts[g * gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS + gltf::AT_WEIGHT + k]` for k in 4), take the slot with the largest sum, its node `gltf::ints[gltf::skins[sk_i].joints.first + slot]`, and push `region(gltf::text_of(gltf::nodes[node].name))`.

`cor_build(asset int, name const byte[:])` computes centers of rotation (Le and Hodgins 2016) for the vertices of mesh name. Source triangles come from mesh name and, when name is not "skin", also from mesh "skin" (find each with `gltf::find_node` and walk its primitives as gather does). For each source triangle keep its rest centroid, its rest area and its averaged weights: the three corners' (joint, weight) pairs merged by joint into at most 12 pairs, each weight divided by 3. Size CR and CH to `gltf::verts.len / gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS`. For each vertex g of mesh name collect its influences with weight > 0; when fewer than two, CH[g] stays false. Otherwise sum over all source triangles: the similarity s is the sum over every pair j < k of the vertex's influences (joints a and b with vertex weights wa and wb) of `wa * wb * ta * tb * exp(-((wa * tb - wb * ta) * (wa * tb - wb * ta)) / (0.1 * 0.1))`, where ta and tb are the triangle's averaged weights for joints a and b (skip the pair when either is 0); add `s * area * centroid` to a float3 numerator and `s * area` to a denominator (accumulate both in real). CH[g] is true when the denominator exceeds 1.0e-12 and then `CR[g]` is numerator over denominator. Print "cor: ", how many vertices got a center, " of ", how many were examined, " from ", the source triangle count, " triangles". Call `s3d::pose(it)` then `motion::joints(sk_i, pal)`; when cor_on, resize JQ to pal.len and set `JQ[k] = spring::mquat(pal[k])`. Make three local `int[>..]` arrays fo, cr and st, each resized to NB zeros, and totals F, C, X. For each triangle t with ra[t] > 1.0e-10: skinned corner points pa, pb, pc from `skp(id, pal[..])`; `ng = linalg::cross(pb - pa, pc - pa)`; area `0.5 * linalg::length3(ng)`; reference normal `nr = skn(i0, pal[..]) + skn(i1, pal[..]) + skn(i2, pal[..])`. The triangle is folded when `linalg::dot3(ng, nr) < 0.0`, crushed when area < 0.3 * ra[t], stretched when area > 2.5 * ra[t]; count each in its region rb[t] and in its total; when dump is true, the tag starts with "Sitting_Idle_Loop 2" and rb[t] == 0, print "F " (folded) or "C " (crushed, when not folded) for such triangles followed by the rest centroid x, y and z separated by spaces. Print `tag, " folded ", F, " crushed ", C, " stretched ", X, " of ", bt.len / 3`. Then for each region k from 0 to NB - 1 where fo[k] + cr[k] + st[k] > 0, print `"  ", rname(k), " folded ", fo[k], " crushed ", cr[k], " stretched ", st[k]`.

`world_rot(nd int) linalg::Quat` is the bind-pose world rotation of node nd: the product of `gltf::nodes[k].r` from the root down to nd, walking `gltf::nodes[k].parent` up (negative ends) and composing with `linalg::qmul(parent, child)`.

`move_joint(asset int, spec const byte[:])` moves one joint's pivot in the bind pose while every other joint keeps its world position. spec is "name:dx,dy,dz" in meters, world axes; split it at the colon and the commas and parse the reals with `parse_flt`. Find the node with `gltf::find_node(asset, name)` (print "no joint " and the name and return when negative). Let d be the world delta. Add `linalg::qrotate(linalg::qconj(world_rot(parent)), d)` to `gltf::nodes[nd].t` (use the identity rotation when the parent is negative). For each child c (`gltf::ints[ch.first + k]` for k in `gltf::nodes[nd].children.count`) subtract `linalg::qrotate(linalg::qconj(world_rot(nd)), d)` from `gltf::nodes[c].t`. For every skin s of the asset (`gltf::assets[asset].skins`, global index first plus k) and every joint slot k of it whose node `gltf::ints[gltf::skins[s].joints.first + k]` is nd, replace the inverse bind m = `gltf::matrices[gltf::skins[s].inverse_binds.first + k]` with `gfx::mul(gfx::translate(float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 } - (linalg::point(m, d) - linalg::point(m, float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 }))), m)`. Print "moved " and the name.

`find_clip(name const byte[:], n int) int` returns the first clip c below n whose name equals name, else -1: for each c clear a reusable `byte[>..]` buffer, call `clips::clips_name(c, buf)` and compare `buf == name`.

`main()`. `let a = args()`; when `a.len < 3` print "usage: fold_check <model.glb> <clips.gltf> [mesh=skin] [move=joint:dx,dy,dz ...] [dump] [cor] [half] [knee=k] [elbow=k]; counts folded, crushed and stretched triangles per body region in bind, idle, walk, dance and sit poses" and return; first `clips::clips_lib(a[2])` (the library loads before the model so the model stays the last asset, as in the viewer), then `let asset = gltf::load(a[1])` (when negative print "load fail" and return); for every argument from index 3 on that starts with "move=", `move_joint(asset, the rest of it)`; then `let it = s3d::add(asset)`; `let nlib = clips::clips_load(a[2], asset)`. Build the slot table exactly so: `var sl i32[22]; let first = gltf::assets[asset].nodes.first; for i in 22 { sl[i] = if clips::kc_slot[i] < 0 { -1 } else { (clips::kc_slot[i] as int - first) as i32 }; }`, then call the unqualified `mix_open(asset, it, sl[..])` and for c in nlib the unqualified `mix_clip(clips::kc_nf[c], clips::kc_loop[c], clips::clips_frames(c))`. Set dump when any argument from index 3 on equals "dump" and cor_on when one equals "cor"; when one equals "half", right after building the slot table and before `mix_open`, call the unqualified `half_joints(asset, hk[..], hs[..])` with locals `var hk int[6]` holding `clips::kc_slot[14]`, `clips::kc_slot[18]`, `clips::kc_slot[8]`, `clips::kc_slot[12]`, `clips::kc_slot[15]` and `clips::kc_slot[19]` as int (hips, elbows, knees) and `var hs f32[6]` holding hp, hp, ek, ek, -kk, -kk, where hp, ek and kk are the numbers after "hip=", "elbow=" and "knee=" in an argument from index 3 on (hp defaults to 0.0, plain half joints at the hips) (parsed as move_joint parses its numbers; ek defaults to 2.0 and kk to 3.0, the viewer's values: crease helpers reaching 2 radii at the elbows, which fold toward +z, and 3 radii at the knees, which fold toward -z; 0 gives that joint a plain half joint); when kk is negative set hk[4] and hk[5] to -1 and hs[4] and hs[5] to 0.0 (no knee helpers); print "half joints " and its result. When an argument from index 3 on equals "twist", right after that (still before `mix_open`) call the unqualified `twist_joints(asset, tk[..])` with a local `var tk int[2]` holding `clips::kc_slot[8]` and `clips::kc_slot[12]` as int (the lower arms) and print "twist joints " and its result. The mesh name is the first argument from index 3 on that neither starts with "move=" nor "knee=" nor "elbow=" nor "hip=" nor equals "dump", "cor", "half" or "twist", else "skin". Call `gather(asset, that name)`; when bt is empty return; when cor_on call `cor_build(asset, that name)`. Print `"skin tris ", bt.len / 3, " height ", h0, " to ", h1, " clips ", nlib`. Call `measure(it, "bind")`. Then the clip schedule: names `["Idle_Loop", "Walk_Formal_Loop", "Dance_Loop", "Sitting_Idle_Loop"]` with sample times `[[1.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], [0.5, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0], [0.7, 1.4, 2.1, 2.8], [1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 0.0]]`. For each clip index ci: `let c = find_clip(names[ci], nlib)`; when c < 0 print "no clip " and the name and continue; call the unqualified `mix_play(c, 0.0)` and keep a local time `var t f32 = 0.0`; for si in 4 with `let target = at[ci][si]` (skip when target <= 0.0): while `t + 0.0001 < target` call the unqualified `mix_advance(1.0 / 60.0)` and add 1.0 / 60.0 to t; then build a tag (the clip name, a space, `str(target)`) and call `measure(it, tag)`. Last, the hands turned over: for each angle ang of -1.4 and 1.4 (f32): call the unqualified `mix_rest()`; for each hand slot k of 9 and 13 with `slot_node[k] >= 0` (the mixer's slot_node and rest_q, unqualified): call the unqualified `mix_set(k, linalg::qmul(linalg::qaxis(linalg::unit3(gltf::nodes[slot_node[k]].t), ang), rest_q[k]))`; then the unqualified `push()`, and `measure(it, "hands turned -1.4")` or `measure(it, "hands turned 1.4")`.
